appnid:pc_PC1 a skos:Concept,
        appn:PhysicalContainmentLevel ;
    dcterms:description """A facility certified as a PC 1 Facility is appropriate for the conduct of the dealings listed below, provided it meets the specific requirements described in the PC 1 Facility guidelines for the dealing type:

- GM micro-organisms (when there is less than or equal to 25 litres of culture of any one GMO);
- GM animals (whether or not they contain microorganisms) as permitted by the Gene Technology Regulations 2001;
- non GM animals containing GM micro-organisms; and
- non-GM plants that contain or host GMOs.

A PC 1 Facility is not appropriate for the following:

- dealings with any GMO that under the Act, or under the conditions of a licence, requires containment in any PC level higher than PC 1.""" ;
    dcterms:title "PC1" ;
    schema:description """A facility certified as a PC 1 Facility is appropriate for the conduct of the dealings listed below, provided it meets the specific requirements described in the PC 1 Facility guidelines for the dealing type:

- GM micro-organisms (when there is less than or equal to 25 litres of culture of any one GMO);
- GM animals (whether or not they contain microorganisms) as permitted by the Gene Technology Regulations 2001;
- non GM animals containing GM micro-organisms; and
- non-GM plants that contain or host GMOs.

A PC 1 Facility is not appropriate for the following:

- dealings with any GMO that under the Act, or under the conditions of a licence, requires containment in any PC level higher than PC 1.""" ;
    schema:name "PC1" ;
    skos:altLabel "Physical Containment Level 1" ;
    skos:inScheme appnid:cs_PhysicalContainmentLevel ;
    skos:prefLabel "PC1 (PhysicalContainmentLevel)" .

appnid:pc_PC2 a skos:Concept,
        appn:PhysicalContainmentLevel ;
    dcterms:description """A facility certified as a PC 2 Plant Facility is appropriate for the conduct of the dealings listed below:

- the growing of GM terrestrial plants; or
- the growing of terrestrial plants that contain GMOs.

A PC 2 Plant Facility is not appropriate for the following:

- dealings with any GMO that under the conditions of a licence or legislation requires containment in any PC level higher than PC 2;
- the housing/keeping/rearing of any animals, invertebrates, or aquatic organisms unless they are integral to the dealing being contained in the facility;
- dealings producing more than 25 litres of liquid culture of GMOs in each vessel; or
- any other work prohibited in writing by the Regulator.""" ;
    dcterms:title "PC2" ;
    schema:description """A facility certified as a PC 2 Plant Facility is appropriate for the conduct of the dealings listed below:

- the growing of GM terrestrial plants; or
- the growing of terrestrial plants that contain GMOs.

A PC 2 Plant Facility is not appropriate for the following:

- dealings with any GMO that under the conditions of a licence or legislation requires containment in any PC level higher than PC 2;
- the housing/keeping/rearing of any animals, invertebrates, or aquatic organisms unless they are integral to the dealing being contained in the facility;
- dealings producing more than 25 litres of liquid culture of GMOs in each vessel; or
- any other work prohibited in writing by the Regulator.""" ;
    schema:name "PC2" ;
    skos:altLabel "Physical Containment Level 2" ;
    skos:inScheme appnid:cs_PhysicalContainmentLevel ;
    skos:prefLabel "PC2 (PhysicalContainmentLevel)" .

appnid:pc_PC3 a skos:Concept,
        appn:PhysicalContainmentLevel ;
    dcterms:description """A facility certified as a PC 3 Facility is appropriate for the conduct of the dealings listed below:

- dealings with GM micro-organisms;
- laboratory procedures involving small terrestrial animals and invertebrates, if not otherwise prohibited by licence conditions;
- laboratory procedures involving aquatic organisms (including amphibians), subject to additional conditions and if not otherwise prohibited by licence conditions.

A PC 3 Facility is not appropriate for the following:

- dealings with any GMO that, under the gene technology legislation or conditions of a licence, require containment in a physical containment level higher than PC3;
- dealings involving a micro-organism that satisfies the criteria in AS/NZS 2243.3 for classification as Risk Group 4;
- the housing/keeping/rearing of any plants, animals, including invertebrates and aquatic organisms, beyond the minimum time that they are required for conducting the dealings with GMOs; or
- any other work prohibited by notification in writing by the Regulator.""" ;
    dcterms:title "PC3" ;
    schema:description """A facility certified as a PC 3 Facility is appropriate for the conduct of the dealings listed below:

- dealings with GM micro-organisms;
- laboratory procedures involving small terrestrial animals and invertebrates, if not otherwise prohibited by licence conditions;
- laboratory procedures involving aquatic organisms (including amphibians), subject to additional conditions and if not otherwise prohibited by licence conditions.

A PC 3 Facility is not appropriate for the following:

- dealings with any GMO that, under the gene technology legislation or conditions of a licence, require containment in a physical containment level higher than PC3;
- dealings involving a micro-organism that satisfies the criteria in AS/NZS 2243.3 for classification as Risk Group 4;
- the housing/keeping/rearing of any plants, animals, including invertebrates and aquatic organisms, beyond the minimum time that they are required for conducting the dealings with GMOs; or
- any other work prohibited by notification in writing by the Regulator.""" ;
    schema:name "PC3" ;
    skos:altLabel "Physical Containment Level 3" ;
    skos:inScheme appnid:cs_PhysicalContainmentLevel ;
    skos:prefLabel "PC3 (PhysicalContainmentLevel)" .

appnid:pc_PC4 a skos:Concept,
        appn:PhysicalContainmentLevel ;
    dcterms:description """A facility certified as a PC 4 Facility is appropriate for the conduct of dealings that are authorised by a licence requiring this level of containment This generally involves organisms classified as Risk group 4, or Risk group 3 (RG3) organisms which have been modified and as a result are more harmful than the RG3 parent organism. Dealings permitted to be conducted
within the facility are therefore the result of an extensive risk assessment of proposed projects and the mandatory implementation of a risk management plan through licence conditions.

The Guidelines contains the requirement for certification of a PC 4 Facility to be certified, and the conditions a facility must continue to comply for the facility to remain certified. Given the type of dealings conducted within the facility and the characteristics of the facility, bespoke requirements and conditions are likely to be included in the certification instrument.""" ;
    dcterms:title "PC4" ;
    schema:description """A facility certified as a PC 4 Facility is appropriate for the conduct of dealings that are authorised by a licence requiring this level of containment This generally involves organisms classified as Risk group 4, or Risk group 3 (RG3) organisms which have been modified and as a result are more harmful than the RG3 parent organism. Dealings permitted to be conducted
within the facility are therefore the result of an extensive risk assessment of proposed projects and the mandatory implementation of a risk management plan through licence conditions.

The Guidelines contains the requirement for certification of a PC 4 Facility to be certified, and the conditions a facility must continue to comply for the facility to remain certified. Given the type of dealings conducted within the facility and the characteristics of the facility, bespoke requirements and conditions are likely to be included in the certification instrument.""" ;
    schema:name "PC4" ;
    skos:altLabel "Physical Containment Level 4" ;
    skos:inScheme appnid:cs_PhysicalContainmentLevel ;
    skos:prefLabel "PC4 (PhysicalContainmentLevel)" .

